// IMapSetRetain -- ARC Task 5's retaining sibling of IMapSet, chosen by
// lowIndexAssign (lower.cla) whenever the stored value is NON-birth. Both
// names share cprint.cla's single printer branch: `m[k] = v` is an UPSERT,
// so the printer ALWAYS emits a has/get/release guard for the value CURRENTLY
// at k (if any) before storing, regardless of which name was chosen -- only
// the new value's retain is conditional on IMapSetRetain vs IMapSet. See
// fpMapReleaseGuard's own doc comment for why the guard's own read is a raw,
// non-retaining rt_map_get (never the retaining IMapGet intrinsic, which
// would leave the guard's own release netting to a no-op instead of the
// intended -1).
func IMapSetRetain(): int {
    return intern("map_set_retain")
}

