// IMapGetDvBirth -- ARC Task 8 fix (known open leak bug 2): the retaining
// sibling of IMapGetDv, chosen by lowMapMethod (lower.cla) whenever the
// default-value argument is BIRTH (lowElemIsBirth, the SAME birth-vs-retain
// rule every other counted store site uses) -- a freshly constructed,
// independently owned value with no other owner. IMapGetDv's own printer
// always retains its result unconditionally and never releases the default
// argument's own box, which is correct ONLY for a non-birth default (some
// other slot already owns it, so t needs its own +1 either way and the
// default's original box is never orphaned); for a BIRTH default it
// double-retains when the key is absent (leak: dv's own +1 plus an
// unnecessary extra one) and orphans dv's box entirely when the key is
// present (leak: nothing ever releases it). See cprint.cla's own
// IMapGetDvBirth printer for the runtime-conditional fix.
func IMapGetDvBirth(): int {
    return intern("map_get_dv_birth")
}

