// -- retain/release (ARC Task 2) --
// IRetain/IRelease each take one expression argument (the reference to
// retain/release), typed by that argument's own IR type -- never a result
// (void), printed via cprint.cla's fpIntrCall as a bare statement, same
// statement-position shape as ITextStore. A KText/KList/KMap argument
// prints as a direct rt_*_retain/rt_*_release call; a KRec argument prints
// as a call to that record type's generated clar_retain_NAME/
// clar_release_NAME walk helper (cpEmitRcWalks), marking the record type
// needed the first time it's seen. lower.cla doesn't emit either intrinsic
// yet -- inserted starting with a later ARC task -- so this plumbing is
// dormant until then.
func IRetain(): int {
    return intern("retain")
}

